Some days ago Frank Mittelbach asked (on math-font-discuss) for a version o=
f
nfssfont.tex which understands NFSS font specs. Since I had to look
at nfssfont.tex anyway, I gave it a try. The result is attached to this
message. The new commands are \nfssspec, \nfssinfo and \nfssinit.
The command \nfssinfo offers a way to study the NFSS tables interactively.=
=20

I hope this is useful to someone and not off-topic on this list.

Regards, Matthias

